    "tacticalNote": "Haiti relies on defensive organization in a compact 4-4-2, limiting space centrally and looking to hit on the break. They lack individual quality to take on Brazil or Morocco through possession, so their approach is to frustrate, defend deep, and use the transition. They're capable of making any opponent work for their goals.",
    "strength": "Collective spirit and defensive organization — this team will not lie down against anyone, and their emotional connection to representing Haiti creates an intensity that can compensate for technical gaps.",
    "vulnerability": "Quality gap against elite opposition — Brazil and Morocco have the individual quality to unlock any organized defense given enough time on the ball."
  },
  "watchFor": [
    "Haiti's defensive shape under pressure — how long they can hold a low block against Brazil and Morocco will tell you everything about their character.",
